# Track B — Employee mobile My Payroll (learned 2026-08-27)

**Status:** Backlog only. Implement when user explicitly starts **「Track B 시작」**. Do not build on Track A IndexedDB as a fake “phone portal.”

## Problem learned from Track A (current truth)

| Fact | Implication |
|------|-------------|
| Ledger + HR + payslips live in **browser IndexedDB per origin** | Personal phone ≠ company PC data |
| Staff `/employee/login` reads **local** employee rows | Phone Staff login fails or shows empty My Payroll |
| Full **Import Backup** onto a phone | Wrong — exposes full company ledger + other employees |
| Payslip PDF download on company PC | Current workaround (admin/employee on official machine) |

User expectation for later: **employees check personal payslips / timesheets on their own phone** without importing the company backup.

## Track B product requirement (must ship with B auth/storage)

**Employee self-service on personal devices** is a **first-class Track B feature**, not an afterthought.

### Invariant

An authenticated **employee** (or payroll-scoped user) must be able to open My Payroll on a **personal phone or home browser** and see **only their own** HR/payslip/timesheet data from the **server-backed tenant**, with **no** requirement to Import Backup or share the company PIN/ledger PC.

### Required capabilities

1. **Server-backed employee identity** — Employee ID + password (or magic link / SSO later) stored/verified on server for that tenant — not only IndexedDB hash on one PC.  
2. **Mobile-usable My Payroll** — Responsive Staff / My Payroll UI on phone browsers (payslips list, download/view payslip, timesheet entry if product keeps it).  
3. **Least privilege** — Employee token must **not** unlock full accounting (statements, cash, other employees, BAS, backups). Separate roles: `tenant_admin` / `accountant` vs `employee`.  
4. **No full-ledger sync to phone** — Phone gets employee-scoped API responses only; never “restore company backup to mobile.”  
5. **Deactivate on turnover** — Leaving employee’s server login disabled; replacement gets new credentials (same ops intent as Track A HR deactivate + Add).  
6. **Optional notify** — Email/push when payslip published (nice-to-have after core read path).

### Explicit non-goals (do not “solve” mobile this way)

- Instruct staff to Import company backup on personal devices  
- Share company Selpic A PIN as “employee login”  
- Rely on unsigned homepage SSO alone as the phone employee portal  
- Copy entire tenant IndexedDB into mobile Safari/Chrome as the product model  

### Edge cases to design for when building B

- Employee opens prod URL on phone with empty local cache → must still work via API  
- Two employees same phone browser → session isolation / logout clear  
- Accountant PC offline vs phone online → server is SSOT for payslips the employee sees  
- Tenant A employee must never see Tenant B payslips  
- Deactivated / terminated employee → login rejected; old sessions invalidated  
- Password reset without admin sitting at company PC (email reset or admin portal)  
- Payslip PDF generation: server or client from API payload — must not require local HR IndexedDB  

### Suggested placement in Track B build order

After **tenancy & storage** and **real auth**, before or with **onboarding polish**:

1. Tenancy & server ledger  
2. Auth (tenant admin + **employee role**)  
3. **Employee mobile My Payroll API + UI** ← this requirement  
4. Onboarding / harden analyze / billing  

### Acceptance checks (when B is built)

- [ ] Fresh phone browser, no Import → employee login succeeds against server  
- [ ] Sees only own payslips/timesheets  
- [ ] Cannot open full Dashboard ledger with employee credentials  
- [ ] Second employee on same device after logout sees only their data  
- [ ] Deactivated employee cannot log in  
- [ ] Company PC Import/backup remains admin ops — not required for staff phones  

